From 68d2c0f889d135984d59e1acd865ab7c712446bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aryan Randeriya <aryan.k.randeriya@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:53:59 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] fix(js): report an unhandled script exception as an
 exception, not a console.error

HTML "report an exception" fires onerror and the error event and, when no
handler handled it, sends the exception to the developer console. Obscura did
that and also called console.error("Uncaught ... (url:line:col)"), so CDP
clients got a Runtime.consoleAPICalled the page never made next to the
Runtime.exceptionThrown. It also sent exceptionThrown for a document script's
exception that a handler had cancelled, and never sent one for inserted or
timer-string scripts.

report_script_exception now owns the console report: the realm's reporter
returns whether the error was handled, and when it was not, the host queues
Runtime.exceptionThrown (and the MCP console line). A document script's host
path records the exception itself only when the script is not reported.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
